From b5f6446adbcda80575016cbb4eb63c9b1965f358 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhymabek Roman <s.salkimbaev@abaiuniversity.edu.kz>
Date: Sat, 13 Jun 2026 14:24:46 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ntdll: ALPC connection handshake for CoreMessaging

- Implement NtAlpcQueryInformation (AlpcBasicInformation) so CoreMessaging's
  post-create query succeeds instead of taking a failure path.
- Fix NtAlpcSendWaitReceivePort to record the received size on the iosb when a
  queued message is delivered inline (non-pending), so the connect-notification
  synthesis runs for the in-process registrar case.
- Use LPC_CONNECTION_REQUEST = 10 (was 11): CoreMessaging's dispatcher routes
  type 10 to NtAlpcAcceptConnectPort (building its own channel object); type 11
  went down a context-dereferencing path and crashed.

With these, WhatsApp's CoreMessaging registrar completes the full connect ->
receive -> accept handshake. ALPC connect/accept/send/receive roundtrip verified.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
